md`# brain-kernel

The Worker at the Brain's address. It serves the notebook, signs people in with atproto, works out who is calling, and forwards everything else to the core with that answer attached.

It holds no application logic. The caller it names is one of \`owner\`, \`token:NAME\`, a DID, or \`anonymous\`, and nothing a caller sends can set it.

## People

A person is an atproto account, named by its DID. There are two roles. The **owner** is the DID this Brain was installed for. A **member** is a DID the owner added. Anyone else who signs in is nobody.

| a caller | may call |
|---|---|
| the owner, in their own tab | everything |
| the owner, through a turn token or a PDS | everything but \`infra.*\`, \`secret.get\`, \`token.*\`, \`grant.*\`, \`people.put\`, \`people.remove\`, \`people.link\`, \`people.unlink\`, \`rule.put\`, \`rule.delete\` |
| a member | \`inbox.reply\`, \`static.*\`, \`blob.*\`, \`portal.token\`, \`portal.modules\`, \`member.whoami\`, \`member.services\`, \`member.deploy\`, \`member.remove\`, \`member.modules\`, any method of a member's service (\`com.lopecode.brain.m.…\`, decided by its rule in the core), and the methods of their own grant (\`grant.put\`) |
| a DID that is not a member | the methods of its grant |
| anyone, through a portal token | the methods of one member's Workers, as themselves (see Portals) |
| anyone, on a method outside \`com.lopecode.brain\` | that method, as \`anonymous\`. A token sent with it is not read. |

| | |
|---|---|
| \`people.list\` | query, owner. \`{ people }\`: each \`{ did, handle, role, name, addresses, methods }\`. \`role\` is \`owner\`, \`member\` or \`null\` (linked an address, not added). |
| \`people.put\` | procedure, owner's session. \`{ did, name, services, quota, tags }\` makes that DID a member; a field left out keeps what it was. \`services: false\` stops their deploys. \`quota\` is \`{ workers, bytes, calls }\`. \`tags\` is \`[{ tag, access: "read" | "write" }]\`, the file tags they may read or change beside their own. |
| \`people.remove\` | procedure, owner's session. \`{ did }\` removes the member, their grant and their addresses, and has the deployer delete their Workers. Their files stay, for the owner. |
| \`member.deploy\`, \`member.remove\`, \`member.modules\` | procedure, a member. Passed to the deployer with the caller's DID as the author; the owner is refused and deploys with \`infra.apply\`. \`member.deploy\` takes \`{ module, source }\`. |
| \`people.link\` | procedure, owner's session. \`{ channel, address, did }\` binds an address without the sign-in below. |
| \`people.unlink\` | procedure, owner's session. \`{ channel, address }\` |
| Storage | \`rows\`: \`member/<did>\`, \`address/<channel>/<address>\`, \`grant/<did>\`, \`handle/<did>\` |

**Addresses.** A channel is a Worker \`brain-x-NAME\` that appends what it receives to the inbox with \`body.address\`, the sender as that channel knows them (a phone number for \`whatsapp\`). The channel says nothing else about the sender. Which DID an address belongs to is decided here: \`address/NAME/<address>\`, where \`NAME\` comes from the Worker the core named as the entry's sender, not from anything in the entry. A channel can therefore speak only for addresses on its own channel.

**DIDs as addresses.** On \`bluesky\` the address is the sender's DID. \`people.put\` writes \`address/bluesky/<did>\` for the member it adds, and the owner's DID is the owner's without a row. Each change to People sends \`bluesky.know { all }\`, the DIDs of every member, to \`brain-x-bluesky\`. The rows are the kernel's own, which no Worker can read or write, and they are read under the name of the Worker the core identified by its key: an entry from \`brain-x-evil\` carrying the owner's DID is looked up as \`address/evil/<did>\` and names nobody.

**Linking.** A channel sends a stranger \`https://HOST/link?channel=NAME&code=CODE\`. The page asks them to sign in with atproto, shows the address the code stands for, and binds it to the signed-in DID when they press Link. The kernel learns the address by calling the channel's \`NAME.claim\` with the code; the answer is taken only from the Worker \`brain-x-NAME\`. Linking does not make anyone a member.

**Turns.** \`inbox.list\` and \`inbox.poll\` answers pass through the kernel, which adds \`who: { did, role, handle }\` to each entry whose address is linked. For the owner's own session \`inbox.poll\` also adds \`turn\`, a token for each entry whose sender is the owner or a member. A call that carries it as \`Authorization: Bearer\` is made as that DID, with \`x-brain-via: turn:<entry id>\`. It lasts 10 minutes, ends with "sign out everywhere", and is refused once its DID is no longer a member.

**Rooms.** A channel's entry may carry \`body.room: { id, name, members }\`: the message was written where others read the answer, and \`members\` are their addresses on that channel. A turn for such an entry is capped by who is in the room, because its answer is read by all of them.

| in the room | the turn may call |
|---|---|
| the sender alone | what the sender may |
| anyone else | \`inbox.reply\`, and a method only when the sender and every other participant has it: the owner has every method, a member the methods of their grant, anyone else none |

So the owner being in a room raises nothing, one participant who is not a member leaves \`inbox.reply\` alone, and the methods every member has by default (\`static.*\`, \`blob.*\`, \`member.*\`, a member's own services) are refused in a room: they answer with the caller's own files and services, which the others in the room cannot read. No path that is not a method is served to a room's turn.

When \`inbox.poll\` hands out the turn, the kernel asks the channel for the room as it is then (\`NAME.room { id }\`, answered only by \`brain-x-NAME\`) and resolves each address as it resolves a sender. The DIDs go into the turn token; member rows and grants are read at each call, so a grant withdrawn or a member removed during a turn is refused from then on. A channel that does not answer, a list that leaves out the sender, one marked incomplete or longer than 50: each counts as a participant who is not a member. A room the channel says it no longer serves gets no turn. The entry gains \`room: { id, name, served, people }\` for the page.

A channel can narrow a turn with this and cannot widen one: the cap is taken inside what the sender may call, and the sender is still found under the channel's own name.

**Members in the core.** After \`people.put\`, \`people.remove\`, \`grant.put\` and \`grant.delete\` the kernel sends the core every member with their grant, limits and tags (\`people.sync\`), because the core checks a member's Worker as its author.

**Sessions.** No cookie is set or read. After atproto sign-in \`/auth/callback\` answers a page that writes a session token to this origin's \`localStorage\` (\`brain_session\`) and goes on; the Brain's page sends it as \`Authorization: Bearer\` with every call. It is a signed \`{ did, exp, epoch }\`, lasts 30 days and is not renewed: after that the visitor signs in again. "Sign out" drops it from the page; "sign out everywhere" (\`/auth/logout?everywhere=true\`) raises the epoch, which ends every session, turn and portal token issued before. Because a caller is only ever who their token says, a page on another address has nothing of this Brain's to send, and \`Origin\` is not looked at. A link or an \`<img>\` cannot carry a token: a private file is fetched by the page and shown from the bytes. The secret that signs all three kinds of token is still named \`COOKIE_KEY\`.

Before 2026-10-07 13:40 the session was a \`SameSite=Lax\` cookie. \`NAME.SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev\` addresses are one site, so a page on another Worker's address sent it: on cb4 the owner's cookie with \`Origin: https://evil.endpointservices.workers.dev\` got 200 from \`GET library.list\` and \`POST token.revoke\`.

**Portals.** \`portal.token { author }\`, called with a session by the owner or a member, answers \`{ token, author, id, expires }\`: a 10-minute token naming the caller as the viewer and one member as the author. A call carrying it is made as the viewer with \`x-brain-via: portal:<id>\`, and reaches only the methods of that member's Workers (\`com.lopecode.brain.m.<id>.…\`, where the Worker's own rule then decides) and \`portal.modules\`, which answers that member's module sources and \`cloudflare-iac\`. When the viewer is the author it also reaches \`member.whoami\`, \`member.services\`, \`member.deploy\`, \`member.remove\` and \`member.modules\`. It is refused once the viewer or the author is no longer a member. The page gives it to a sandboxed frame (\`brain-shell\`, "Portals"), so a member's code never holds the viewer's session.

Limits: an entry is stamped when it is read, so an address linked after its message arrived is known from then on. The kernel does not record which turn made a call.`
// %%
kernel_service = cloudflare.Service("kernel", kernelApp, { role: "kernel" })
// %%
// Announced to the page, so the Services list shows it. A cell of its own: a deployed function cannot depend on it.
kernel_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", kernel_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced kernel_service";
}
// %%
// @atcute's OAuth client, identity resolvers and signature check as one ES module (77 KB). Travels as lib/atcute.js.
atcute = library("atcute", FileAttachment("atcute.js"))
// %%
// A page's session: a signed note of who signed in, which the page keeps and sends as Authorization: Bearer.
// The atproto tokens stay in the kernel's rows.
sessionToken = {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const b64u = (bytes) => btoa(String.fromCharCode(...bytes)).replace(/\+/g, "-").replace(/\//g, "_").replace(/=+$/, "");
  const sign = async (key, text) => {
    const k = await crypto.subtle.importKey("raw", enc.encode(key), { name: "HMAC", hash: "SHA-256" }, false, ["sign"]);
    return b64u(new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.sign("HMAC", k, enc.encode(text))));
  };
  return {
    make: async (key, did, { ttl = 30 * 24 * 3600 * 1000, epoch = 0 } = {}) => {
      const payload = b64u(enc.encode(JSON.stringify({ did, exp: Date.now() + ttl, epoch })));
      return `v1.${payload}.${await sign(key, payload)}`;
    },
    read: async (key, token, epoch = 0) => {
      const [v, payload, sig] = String(token || "").split(".");
      if (v !== "v1" || !key || !payload || sig !== (await sign(key, payload))) return null;
      try {
        const claims = JSON.parse(atob(payload.replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/")));
        return claims.exp > Date.now() && (claims.epoch || 0) === epoch ? claims.did : null;
      } catch {
        return null;
      }
    }
  };
}
// %%
// One inbox entry's turn: who it is for and which entry, signed with the session key under its own label.
turnToken = {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const b64u = (bytes) => btoa(String.fromCharCode(...bytes)).replace(/\+/g, "-").replace(/\//g, "_").replace(/=+$/, "");
  const sign = async (key, text) => {
    const k = await crypto.subtle.importKey("raw", enc.encode(key), { name: "HMAC", hash: "SHA-256" }, false, ["sign"]);
    return b64u(new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.sign("HMAC", k, enc.encode("turn:" + text))));
  };
  return {
    // room: the DIDs of everyone else who reads the answer, null for one who is nobody here.
    make: async (key, did, entry, { ttl = 600000, epoch = 0, room } = {}) => {
      const payload = b64u(enc.encode(JSON.stringify({ did, entry, exp: Date.now() + ttl, epoch, ...(room ? { room } : {}) })));
      return `t1.${payload}.${await sign(key, payload)}`;
    },
    read: async (key, token, epoch = 0) => {
      const [v, payload, sig] = String(token || "").split(".");
      if (v !== "t1" || !key || !payload || sig !== (await sign(key, payload))) return null;
      try {
        const claims = JSON.parse(atob(payload.replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/")));
        return claims.exp > Date.now() && (claims.epoch || 0) === epoch ? { did: claims.did, entry: claims.entry, ...(Array.isArray(claims.room) ? { room: claims.room } : {}) } : null;
      } catch {
        return null;
      }
    }
  };
}
// %%
// A portal's token: who is looking (did) and whose services they are looking at (author, and that author's ID).
// Signed with the session key under its own label, so it is neither a session nor a turn.
portalToken = {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const b64u = (bytes) => btoa(String.fromCharCode(...bytes)).replace(/\+/g, "-").replace(/\//g, "_").replace(/=+$/, "");
  const sign = async (key, text) => {
    const k = await crypto.subtle.importKey("raw", enc.encode(key), { name: "HMAC", hash: "SHA-256" }, false, ["sign"]);
    return b64u(new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.sign("HMAC", k, enc.encode("portal:" + text))));
  };
  return {
    make: async (key, did, author, id, { ttl = 600000, epoch = 0 } = {}) => {
      const payload = b64u(enc.encode(JSON.stringify({ did, author, id, exp: Date.now() + ttl, epoch })));
      return `p1.${payload}.${await sign(key, payload)}`;
    },
    read: async (key, token, epoch = 0) => {
      const [v, payload, sig] = String(token || "").split(".");
      if (v !== "p1" || !key || !payload || sig !== (await sign(key, payload))) return null;
      try {
        const claims = JSON.parse(atob(payload.replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/")));
        return claims.exp > Date.now() && (claims.epoch || 0) === epoch ? { did: claims.did, author: claims.author, id: claims.id } : null;
      } catch {
        return null;
      }
    }
  };
}
// %%
// A call forwarded by a PDS carries a JWT signed with the caller's atproto key. Checked against their DID document.
verifyServiceJwt = async (bearer, nsid, audience) => {
  const b64u = (t) => Uint8Array.from(atob(t.replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/").padEnd(Math.ceil(t.length / 4) * 4, "=")), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0));
  const [h, p, s] = bearer.split(".");
  let claims;
  try {
    claims = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(b64u(p)));
  } catch {
    return { error: "BadJwt", message: "not a JWT" };
  }
  if (claims.aud !== audience && claims.aud !== audience + "#brain") return { error: "BadJwtAudience", message: "aud " + claims.aud };
  if (!(claims.exp > Date.now() / 1000)) return { error: "JwtExpired", message: "exp " + claims.exp };
  if (claims.lxm !== nsid) return { error: "BadJwtLexiconMethod", message: "lxm " + claims.lxm };
  if (typeof claims.iss !== "string" || !claims.iss.startsWith("did:")) return { error: "BadJwtIssuer", message: "iss" };
  const resolver = new atcute.CompositeDidDocumentResolver({ methods: { plc: new atcute.PlcDidDocumentResolver(), web: new atcute.WebDidDocumentResolver() } });
  const doc = await resolver.resolve(claims.iss.split("#")[0]);
  const vm = (doc.verificationMethod || []).find((m) => m.id.endsWith("#atproto"));
  if (!vm) return { error: "BadJwtIssuer", message: "no #atproto key" };
  const ok = await atcute.verifySig(atcute.parsePublicMultikey(vm.publicKeyMultibase), b64u(s), new TextEncoder().encode(h + "." + p), { allowMalleableSig: true });
  return ok ? { iss: claims.iss.split("#")[0] } : { error: "BadJwtSignature", message: "signature does not verify" };
}
// %%
kernelApp = {
  const app = new hono.Hono();
  const NS = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.";
  const fail = (c, status, error, message) => c.json({ error, message }, status);
  app.onError((e, c) => fail(c, 500, "InternalServerError", String((e && e.message) || e)));
  // What every member may call. Anything more is that member's grant.
  const MEMBER = ["inbox.reply", "member.whoami", "member.services", "member.deploy", "member.remove", "member.modules", "static.put", "static.get", "static.list", "static.tag", "static.setPublic", "static.delete", "blob.upload", "blob.get", "blob.info", "blob.list", "blob.tag", "blob.delete", "portal.token", "portal.modules", "quota.get"].map((m) => "com.lopecode.brain." + m);
  // What a portal token reaches beside the methods of its author's Workers, when the viewer is that author.
  const PORTAL_OWN = ["member.whoami", "member.services", "member.deploy", "member.remove", "member.modules"].map((m) => "com.lopecode.brain." + m);
  // A method of some member's own service. Its rule, which the deployer wrote, says whether another member may call it.
  const MEMBER_NS = "com.lopecode.brain.m.";

  // Every caller sends a token in a header, this Brain's own page included, so any origin may call and read the answer.
  const cors = { "access-control-allow-origin": "*", "access-control-allow-headers": "authorization, content-type", "access-control-allow-methods": "GET, POST", "access-control-expose-headers": "x-proxy-upstream", "access-control-max-age": "600" };
  app.use("/xrpc/*", async (c, next) => {
    if (c.req.method === "OPTIONS") return new Response(null, { status: 204, headers: cors });
    await next();
    if (!c.req.header("authorization")) return;
    const headers = new Headers(c.res.headers);
    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(cors)) headers.set(k, v);
    c.res = new Response(c.res.body, { status: c.res.status, headers, webSocket: c.res.webSocket });
  });

  // Nothing a browser sends by itself says who is calling: no cookie is read. A caller is whoever their token says.
  // The key that signs session, turn and portal tokens is SESSION_KEY. It was COOKIE_KEY until 2026-10-07, and a
  // Brain installed before then has that name bound. A token is signed with the first name bound and read with either.
  const signingKeys = async () => {
    const bound = async (read) => {
      try {
        return (await read()) || null;
      } catch {
        return null;
      }
    };
    return [...new Set([await bound(() => secrets.SESSION_KEY), await bound(() => secrets.COOKIE_KEY)].filter((k) => typeof k === "string" && k))];
  };
  const signingKey = async () => (await signingKeys())[0];
  const readToken = async (kind, bearer, epoch) => {
    for (const key of await signingKeys()) {
      const read = await kind.read(key, bearer, epoch);
      if (read) return read;
    }
    return null;
  };
  const identify = async (request, nsid) => {
    const auth = request.headers.get("authorization") || "";
    if (!auth.startsWith("Bearer ")) return { caller: "anonymous", via: "" };
    const bearer = auth.slice(7), named = (did) => (did === config.owner ? "owner" : did);
    if (/^[vtp]1\./.test(bearer)) {
      const epoch = (await rows.get("epoch")) || 0;
      if (bearer.startsWith("v1.")) {
        const did = await readToken(sessionToken, bearer, epoch);
        return did ? { caller: named(did), via: "session", did } : { refused: { error: "AuthRequired", message: "this session has expired or is not this Brain's" } };
      }
      if (bearer.startsWith("t1.")) {
        const turn = await readToken(turnToken, bearer, epoch);
        return turn ? { caller: named(turn.did), via: "turn:" + turn.entry, did: turn.did, turn: true, room: turn.room || null } : { refused: { error: "AuthRequired", message: "this turn token has expired or is not this Brain's" } };
      }
      const portal = await readToken(portalToken, bearer, epoch);
      return portal ? { caller: named(portal.did), via: "portal:" + portal.id, did: portal.did, portal } : { refused: { error: "AuthRequired", message: "this portal token has expired or is not this Brain's" } };
    }
    if (bearer.split(".").length === 3) {
      const v = await verifyServiceJwt(bearer, nsid, "did:web:" + config.host);
      return v.error ? { refused: v } : { caller: v.iss === config.owner ? "owner" : v.iss, via: "jwt", did: v.iss };
    }
    const token = await rows.get("token/" + (await sha256(bearer)));
    return token ? { caller: "token:" + token.name, via: "token", methods: token.methods } : { refused: { error: "AuthRequired", message: "unknown token" } };
  };
  app.use("*", async (c, next) => {
    const path = new URL(c.req.url).pathname;
    const nsid = path.startsWith("/xrpc/") ? path.slice("/xrpc/".length) : null;
    // A method outside com.lopecode.brain is another service's lexicon, which this Brain answers to anyone
    // (app.bsky.feed.getFeedSkeleton). Whatever token comes with it is not read, so the caller is anonymous.
    const who = nsid && !nsid.startsWith("com.lopecode.brain.") ? { caller: "anonymous", via: "" } : await identify(c.req.raw, nsid);
    if (who.refused) return fail(c, who.refused.status || 401, who.refused.error, who.refused.message);
    // A token or another DID reaches only the methods it was given, and no path that is not a method.
    if (who.via === "token" && !(nsid && who.methods.includes(nsid))) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "this token does not name " + (nsid || path));
    // A portal shows one member's services to whoever opened it. Its token reaches the methods of that member's
    // Workers and the list of their modules, as the viewer; when the viewer is that member, their own services too.
    if (who.portal) {
      const mine = MEMBER_NS + who.portal.id + ".";
      const reach = nsid && (nsid.startsWith(mine) || nsid === "com.lopecode.brain.portal.modules" || (who.portal.did === who.portal.author && PORTAL_OWN.includes(nsid)));
      if (!reach) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `a portal token reaches ${mine}* and nothing else`);
      if (!(await rows.get("member/" + who.portal.author))) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${who.portal.author} is not a member`);
    }
    // A turn whose answer others read: inbox.reply, and what the sender and every one of them has. The owner has
    // every method, a member their grant, anyone else nothing. Read now, not when the token was made.
    const others = who.turn && who.room ? who.room.filter((d) => d !== who.did) : [];
    // A turn copies a secret only when the owner alone reads the answer.
    if (who.turn && who.room && nsid === "com.lopecode.brain.secret.copy") return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "a turn in a room does not copy a secret");
    if (others.length && nsid !== "com.lopecode.brain.inbox.reply")
      for (const did of [who.did, ...others]) {
        if (did && did === config.owner) continue;
        const grant = did && (await rows.get("member/" + did)) ? await rows.get("grant/" + did) : null;
        if (!(nsid && grant && grant.methods.includes(nsid))) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `a turn in a room reaches inbox.reply and what everyone in the room has a grant for; ${did === who.did ? "its sender" : did || "someone who is not a member"} has none for ${nsid || path}`);
      }
    if (who.caller.startsWith("did:")) {
      const member = await rows.get("member/" + who.caller);
      // A turn is run for a member. Once they are removed, a token already issued stops working.
      if ((who.turn || who.portal) && !member) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${who.caller} is not a member`);
      const grant = nsid ? await rows.get("grant/" + who.caller) : null;
      if (nsid && !(member && (MEMBER.includes(nsid) || nsid.startsWith(MEMBER_NS))) && !(grant && grant.methods.includes(nsid))) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${who.caller} has no grant for ${nsid}`);
      // A member is still themselves when they open a file; every other page is served to them as to anyone.
      if (!nsid && !(member && path.startsWith("/static/"))) who.caller = "anonymous";
    }
    c.set("who", who);
    c.set("nsid", nsid);
    await next();
  });
  const session = async (c, next) =>
    c.get("who").caller === "owner" && c.get("who").via === "session" ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner's own session");
  const owner = async (c, next) => (c.get("who").caller === "owner" ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner"));

  app.get("/.well-known/did.json", (c) =>
    c.json({ "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/did/v1"], id: "did:web:" + config.host, service: [{ id: "#brain", type: "CloudBrain", serviceEndpoint: "https://" + config.host }, { id: "#bsky_fg", type: "BskyFeedGenerator", serviceEndpoint: "https://" + config.host }, ...(config.deployer ? [{ id: "#deployer", type: "CloudBrainDeployer", serviceEndpoint: config.deployer }] : [])] })
  );

  // atproto sign-in, as a confidential client whose key this kernel made.
  const store = (ns) => ({
    get: async (k) => (await rows.get(`oauth/${ns}/${k}`)) ?? undefined,
    set: async (k, v) => void (await rows.put(`oauth/${ns}/${k}`, v)),
    delete: async (k) => void (await rows.delete(`oauth/${ns}/${k}`)),
    clear: async () => {
      for (const r of await rows.list(`oauth/${ns}/`)) await rows.delete(r.key);
    }
  });
  let client = null;
  const oauth = async () => {
    if (client) return client;
    let jwk = await rows.get("oauth/key/main");
    if (!jwk) {
      jwk = await atcute.generateClientAssertionKey("main", "ES256");
      await rows.put("oauth/key/main", jwk);
    }
    const origin = "https://" + config.host + "/auth";
    return (client = new atcute.OAuthClient({
      metadata: { client_id: origin + "/client-metadata.json", redirect_uris: [origin + "/callback"], scope: "atproto transition:generic", jwks_uri: origin + "/jwks.json", client_name: "Cloud Brain " + config.host },
      keyset: [jwk],
      stores: { sessions: store("session"), states: store("state") },
      actorResolver: new atcute.LocalActorResolver({
        handleResolver: new atcute.CompositeHandleResolver({ methods: { dns: new atcute.DohJsonHandleResolver({ dohUrl: "https://mozilla.cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query" }), http: new atcute.WellKnownHandleResolver() } }),
        didDocumentResolver: new atcute.CompositeDidDocumentResolver({ methods: { plc: new atcute.PlcDidDocumentResolver(), web: new atcute.WebDidDocumentResolver() } })
      })
    }));
  };
  app.get("/auth/client-metadata.json", async (c) => c.json((await oauth()).metadata));
  app.get("/auth/jwks.json", async (c) => c.json((await oauth()).jwks));
  app.get("/auth/login", async (c) => {
    const handle = (c.req.query("handle") || "").trim().replace(/^@/, "");
    if (!handle) return c.text("handle", 400);
    // After sign-in a visitor goes back to the link page they came from, and nowhere else.
    const next = c.req.query("next") || "";
    const { url } = await (await oauth()).authorize({ target: { type: "account", identifier: handle }, state: { at: Date.now(), next: /^\/link\?[A-Za-z0-9=&_.-]*$/.test(next) ? next : null } });
    return c.redirect(url.toString(), 302);
  });
  app.get("/auth/callback", async (c) => {
    const client = await oauth();
    const { session, state } = await client.callback(new URL(c.req.url).searchParams);
    const did = session.did;
    let handle = null;
    try {
      const r = await new atcute.Client({ handler: session }).get("com.atproto.server.getSession");
      handle = r.ok ? r.data.handle : null;
    } catch {}
    await rows.put("handle/" + did, handle);
    // Only the owner's atproto session is kept. Anyone else is remembered by DID alone.
    if (did !== config.owner) await client.revoke(did).catch(() => null);
    // The page keeps the session and sends it itself: it is written to this origin's storage and the visitor goes on.
    const token = await sessionToken.make(await signingKey(), did, { epoch: (await rows.get("epoch")) || 0 });
    const body = `try { localStorage.setItem("brain_session", ${JSON.stringify(token)}); location.replace(${JSON.stringify((state && state.next) || "/")}); } catch (e) { document.body.textContent = "This browser would not keep the session: " + e.message; }`;
    return new Response(`<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Signed in</title><body><scr` + `ipt>${body}</scr` + `ipt></body>`, { headers: { "content-type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "cache-control": "no-store", "referrer-policy": "no-referrer", "content-security-policy": "default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'" } });
  });
  app.post("/auth/logout", async (c) => {
    // The page drops its own session. everywhere=true ends every session, turn and portal issued so far.
    if (c.req.query("everywhere") === "true" && c.get("who").caller === "owner" && c.get("who").via === "session") await rows.increment("epoch");
    return new Response(null, { status: 204 });
  });
  app.get("/auth/session", async (c) => {
    const who = c.get("who");
    if (who.via !== "session") return c.json({ signedIn: false, ownerSet: !!config.owner });
    return c.json({ signedIn: true, did: who.did, handle: await rows.get("handle/" + who.did), owner: who.caller === "owner" });
  });

  // Tokens for callers with no session, and grants for other DIDs. Each names the methods it may call.
  const full = (m) => (m.startsWith("com.") ? m : "com.lopecode.brain." + m);
  const never = (m) => /^com\.lopecode\.brain\.(infra|secret|token|grant|people)\./.test(m);
  app.get(NS + "token.list", session, async (c) => c.json({ tokens: (await rows.list("token/")).map((r) => r.value) }));
  app.post(NS + "token.create", session, async (c) => {
    const { name, methods = [] } = await c.req.json();
    const named = methods.map(full);
    if (!/^[a-z0-9-]{1,40}$/.test(name || "")) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "name is lower case letters, digits and -");
    if (named.some(never)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "a token cannot name infra, secret, token, grant or people methods");
    const token = [...crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32))].map((b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
    await rows.put("token/" + (await sha256(token)), { name, methods: named, created: Date.now() });
    return c.json({ name, token });
  });
  app.post(NS + "token.revoke", session, async (c) => {
    const { name } = await c.req.json();
    let revoked = 0;
    for (const r of await rows.list("token/")) if (r.value.name === name) revoked += (await rows.delete(r.key)) ? 1 : 0;
    return c.json({ revoked });
  });
  app.get(NS + "grant.list", session, async (c) => c.json({ grants: (await rows.list("grant/")).map((r) => r.value) }));
  // The core checks a member's Worker as its author, and cannot ask the kernel who that is: it is told, whole, each
  // time a member or a grant changes.
  const syncPeople = async () => {
    const people = [];
    for (const { value: m } of await rows.list("member/")) people.push({ did: m.did, methods: ((await rows.get("grant/" + m.did)) || { methods: [] }).methods, quota: m.quota || null, tags: m.tags || [] });
    await core.fetch(new Request("https://core.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.people.sync", { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": "kernel" }, body: JSON.stringify({ people }) }));
    // A channel that knows senders by DID is told the whole list too; one that is not deployed does not answer.
    for (const channel of NATIVE) await toChannel(channel, "know", { all: people.map((p) => p.did) }).catch(() => null);
  };
  app.post(NS + "grant.put", session, async (c) => {
    const { did, methods = [] } = await c.req.json();
    const named = methods.map(full);
    if (!/^did:(plc|web):[A-Za-z0-9.:%-]+$/.test(did || "")) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "did");
    if (named.some(never) || named.some((m) => m.startsWith("com.lopecode.brain.member."))) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "a grant cannot name infra, secret, token, grant, people or member methods");
    await rows.put("grant/" + did, { did, methods: named, granted: Date.now() });
    await syncPeople();
    return c.json({ did, methods: named });
  });
  app.post(NS + "grant.delete", session, async (c) => {
    const deleted = await rows.delete("grant/" + (await c.req.json()).did);
    await syncPeople();
    return c.json({ deleted });
  });

  // Who is calling, then the core. Nothing the caller sent says who they are.
  const toCore = async (c) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), who = c.get("who");
    const headers = new Headers(c.req.raw.headers);
    for (const name of [...headers.keys()]) if (name === "cookie" || name === "authorization" || name.startsWith("x-brain-")) headers.delete(name);
    headers.set("x-brain-caller", who.caller);
    headers.set("x-brain-via", who.via);
    const bodied = !["GET", "HEAD"].includes(c.req.method);
    return core.fetch(new Request("https://core.internal" + url.pathname + url.search, { method: c.req.method, headers, body: bodied ? c.req.raw.body : undefined, duplex: bodied ? "half" : undefined, redirect: "manual" }));
  };
  // People: members, and which DID an address on a channel belongs to.
  const DID = /^did:(plc|web):[A-Za-z0-9.:%-]+$/, CHANNEL = /^[a-z0-9-]{1,30}$/;
  const addressOk = (a) => typeof a === "string" && a.length > 0 && a.length <= 200 && !a.includes("/");
  const roleOf = async (did) => (did === config.owner ? "owner" : (await rows.get("member/" + did)) ? "member" : null);
  // Channels on which a sender's address is their DID. Nobody links there: a member has the address from the moment
  // they are added, and the owner always.
  const NATIVE = ["bluesky"];
  // A call the kernel makes for itself. Only the Worker named for the channel may answer it.
  const toChannel = async (channel, method, body) => {
    const r = await core.fetch(new Request(`https://core.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.${channel}.${method}`, { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": "kernel" }, body: JSON.stringify(body) }));
    const by = (r.headers.get("x-brain-served-by") || "").split(",")[0].trim();
    if (!r.ok || !by.startsWith(`brain-x-${channel}@`)) return null;
    return r.json().catch(() => null);
  };
  app.get(NS + "people.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const people = new Map();
    const at = (did) => people.get(did) || people.set(did, { did, handle: null, role: null, name: null, added: null, addresses: [], methods: [] }).get(did);
    if (config.owner) at(config.owner).role = "owner";
    for (const { value: m } of await rows.list("member/")) Object.assign(at(m.did), { role: "member", name: m.name || null, added: m.added, services: m.services !== false, quota: m.quota || null, tags: m.tags || [] });
    for (const { value: a } of await rows.list("address/")) at(a.did).addresses.push({ channel: a.channel, address: a.address, linked: a.linked });
    for (const { value: g } of await rows.list("grant/")) if (people.has(g.did)) at(g.did).methods = g.methods;
    for (const p of people.values()) p.handle = await rows.get("handle/" + p.did);
    return c.json({ people: [...people.values()] });
  });
  app.post(NS + "people.put", session, async (c) => {
    const { did, name, services, quota, tags } = await c.req.json();
    if (!DID.test(did || "")) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "did");
    if (did === config.owner) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "the owner is not a member");
    const was = (await rows.get("member/" + did)) || {};
    // quota: { workers, bytes, calls }, each a whole number; a name left out keeps the Brain's default.
    const limits = quota === undefined ? was.quota || null : quota && Object.fromEntries(["workers", "bytes", "calls"].filter((k) => Number.isInteger(quota[k]) && quota[k] >= 0).map((k) => [k, quota[k]]));
    // tags: [{ tag, access: "read" | "write" }], the labels on files this member may read or change beside their own.
    if (tags !== undefined && !(Array.isArray(tags) && tags.length <= 20 && tags.every((g) => g && typeof g.tag === "string" && /^[a-z0-9-]{1,40}$|^(by|worker):[A-Za-z0-9.:%-]{1,120}$/.test(g.tag) && ["read", "write"].includes(g.access)))) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "tags: [{ tag, access: read | write }]");
    await rows.put("member/" + did, { tags: tags === undefined ? was.tags || [] : tags.map((g) => ({ tag: g.tag, access: g.access })), did, name: name === undefined ? was.name || null : name ? String(name).slice(0, 80) : null, added: was.added || Date.now(), services: services === undefined ? was.services !== false : !!services, quota: limits && Object.keys(limits).length ? limits : null });
    for (const channel of NATIVE) if (!(await rows.get(`address/${channel}/${did}`))) await rows.put(`address/${channel}/${did}`, { channel, address: did, did, linked: Date.now() });
    await syncPeople();
    return c.json({ did, role: "member" });
  });
  const unlink = async (channel, address) => {
    const gone = await rows.delete(`address/${channel}/${address}`);
    await toChannel(channel, "know", { address, forget: true });
    return gone;
  };
  app.post(NS + "people.remove", session, async (c) => {
    const { did } = await c.req.json();
    if (!DID.test(did || "") || did === config.owner) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "did");
    const removed = await rows.delete("member/" + did);
    await rows.delete("grant/" + did);
    // From here the core refuses every call into and out of their Workers; the deployer then deletes them.
    await syncPeople();
    await deployer.fetch(new Request("https://deployer.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.member.purge", { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": "owner" }, body: JSON.stringify({ author: did }) })).catch(() => null);
    for (const { value: a } of await rows.list("address/")) if (a.did === did) await unlink(a.channel, a.address);
    return c.json({ removed: !!removed });
  });
  app.post(NS + "people.link", session, async (c) => {
    const { channel, address, did } = await c.req.json();
    if (!CHANNEL.test(channel || "") || !addressOk(address) || !DID.test(did || "")) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "channel, address and did");
    if (!(await toChannel(channel, "know", { address }))) return fail(c, 502, "UpstreamError", `brain-x-${channel} did not answer ${channel}.know`);
    await rows.put(`address/${channel}/${address}`, { channel, address, did, linked: Date.now() });
    return c.json({ channel, address, did, role: await roleOf(did) });
  });
  app.post(NS + "people.unlink", session, async (c) => {
    const { channel, address } = await c.req.json();
    if (!CHANNEL.test(channel || "") || !addressOk(address)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "channel and address");
    return c.json({ unlinked: !!(await unlink(channel, address)) });
  });

  // The page a channel's link opens. Signing in proves the DID, the code proves the address, pressing Link joins them.
  // The page is the same for everyone: its script holds the session, if there is one, and asks with it.
  const linkOf = (q) => (q && CHANNEL.test(q.channel || "") && /^[A-Za-z0-9-]{8,64}$/.test(q.code || "") ? { channel: q.channel, code: q.code } : null);
  const linkScript = `
const app = document.getElementById("app");
const el = (tag, text, attrs) => { const e = document.createElement(tag); if (text) e.textContent = text; for (const k in attrs || {}) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); return e; };
const show = (...nodes) => app.replaceChildren(...nodes);
let token = null; try { token = localStorage.getItem("brain_session"); } catch (e) {}
const call = async (path) => { const r = await fetch(path, { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", authorization: "Bearer " + token }, body: JSON.stringify(LINK) }); return { status: r.status, data: await r.json().catch(() => ({})) }; };
const expired = () => show(el("p", "This link has expired or was already used. Send the Brain another message to get a new one."));
const signIn = () => {
  const form = el("form", "", { method: "get", action: "/auth/login" });
  form.append(el("input", "", { type: "hidden", name: "next", value: "/link?channel=" + LINK.channel + "&code=" + LINK.code }), el("input", "", { name: "handle", placeholder: "you.bsky.social", autocapitalize: "off", autocomplete: "username", style: "font:inherit;padding:6px;width:16em" }), " ", el("button", "Sign in", { style: "font:inherit;padding:6px 12px" }));
  show(el("h3", "Link this " + LINK.channel + " address to a Cloud Brain"), el("p", "Sign in with your atproto (Bluesky) account. You are sent to your own provider to do it; this page never sees your password."), form);
};
const run = async () => {
  if (!LINK) return expired();
  if (!token) return signIn();
  const found = await call("/link/peek");
  if (found.status === 401) return signIn();
  if (found.status !== 200) return expired();
  const go = el("button", "Link", { style: "font:inherit;padding:6px 12px" });
  go.onclick = async () => {
    go.disabled = true;
    const done = await call("/link");
    if (done.status !== 200) return expired();
    show(el("h3", "Linked"), el("p", done.data.role ? "Messages from " + done.data.address + " are now answered." : done.data.address + " is linked to your account. The owner of this Brain has to add you before it answers."));
  };
  show(el("h3", "Link " + LINK.channel + " " + found.data.address + "?"), el("p", "Messages from " + found.data.address + " will be answered as " + found.data.as + "."), el("p", "Only do this if that address is yours and you asked for this link yourself."), go);
};
run();`;
  app.get("/link", (c) =>
    new Response(`<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Link to this Cloud Brain</title><body style="font:16px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:30em;margin:3em auto;padding:0 1em"><div id="app"></div><scr` + `ipt>const LINK = ${JSON.stringify(linkOf(c.req.query()))};${linkScript}</scr` + `ipt></body>`, { headers: { "content-type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "cache-control": "no-store", "referrer-policy": "no-referrer", "content-security-policy": "default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'" } }));
  for (const [path, peek] of [["/link/peek", true], ["/link", false]])
    app.post(path, async (c) => {
      const who = c.get("who");
      if (who.via !== "session" || !who.did) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "sign in first");
      const link = linkOf(await c.req.json().catch(() => null));
      const found = link ? await toChannel(link.channel, "claim", peek ? { code: link.code, peek: true } : { code: link.code }) : null;
      if (!found || !addressOk(found.address)) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", "this link has expired or was already used");
      if (peek) return c.json({ address: found.address, as: ((handle) => (handle ? "@" + handle : who.did))(await rows.get("handle/" + who.did)) });
      await rows.put(`address/${link.channel}/${found.address}`, { channel: link.channel, address: found.address, did: who.did, linked: Date.now() });
      return c.json({ linked: true, address: found.address, role: await roleOf(who.did) });
    });

  // A portal: one member's services, shown to whoever is signed in, in a frame that holds this token and nothing
  // else of theirs. The viewer is named; the reach is that member's Workers.
  app.post(NS + "portal.token", async (c) => {
    const who = c.get("who");
    if (who.via !== "session" || !who.did) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "a signed-in session");
    const { author } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    if (!DID.test(author || "") || !(await rows.get("member/" + author))) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", "no member " + String(author).slice(0, 80));
    const id = (await sha256(author)).slice(0, 10), ttl = 600000;
    return c.json({ token: await portalToken.make(await signingKey(), who.did, author, id, { ttl, epoch: (await rows.get("epoch")) || 0 }), author, id, expires: Date.now() + ttl });
  });
  app.post(NS + "portal.modules", async (c) => {
    const who = c.get("who");
    if (!who.portal) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "a portal token");
    return deployer.fetch(new Request("https://deployer.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.member.modules", { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": "member" }, body: JSON.stringify({ author: who.portal.author, quota: {}, request: {} }) }));
  });

  // A member's own services go to the deployer with the DID that signed in, in a session, a turn, their own portal or through a PDS.
  // The deployer distils the source and decides; nothing here or in a tab evaluates it.
  for (const name of ["deploy", "remove", "modules"])
    app.post(NS + "member." + name, async (c) => {
      const who = c.get("who");
      const member = who.did && who.caller !== "owner" ? await rows.get("member/" + who.did) : null;
      if (!member) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "a member's own services; the owner deploys with infra.apply");
      if (name === "deploy" && member.services === false) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "the owner has switched services off for this member");
      const request = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
      return deployer.fetch(new Request("https://deployer.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.member." + name, { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": "member" }, body: JSON.stringify({ author: who.did, quota: member.quota || {}, request }) }));
    });
  // Deploys go to the deployer, for the owner's own session and nobody else.
  app.all(NS + "infra.*", session, async (c) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), bodied = c.req.method === "POST";
    return deployer.fetch(new Request("https://deployer.internal" + url.pathname + url.search, { method: c.req.method, headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": "owner" }, body: bodied ? c.req.raw.body : undefined, duplex: bodied ? "half" : undefined }));
  });
  // The inbox as a tab reads it: each entry gains who its address belongs to, and for the owner's own
  // session a poll gains a turn token for each entry the owner or a member sent. An entry written in a room
  // gains who is in it, and its token is capped by them.
  for (const [verb, name] of [["get", "inbox.list"], ["post", "inbox.poll"]])
    app[verb](NS + name, async (c) => {
      const r = await toCore(c), who = c.get("who");
      if (!r.ok) return r;
      const data = await r.json().catch(() => null);
      const mint = name === "inbox.poll" && who.caller === "owner" && who.via === "session";
      const key = await signingKey(), epoch = (await rows.get("epoch")) || 0;
      const boundOn = async (channel, address) => (addressOk(address) ? (NATIVE.includes(channel) && address === config.owner ? { did: address } : await rows.get(`address/${channel}/${address}`)) : null);
      for (const e of (data && data.entries) || []) {
        const channel = /^worker:brain-x-([a-z0-9-]+)$/.exec(e.from || ""), address = e.body && e.body.address;
        const bound = channel ? await boundOn(channel[1], address) : null;
        const role = bound ? await roleOf(bound.did) : null;
        e.who = bound ? { did: bound.did, role, handle: await rows.get("handle/" + bound.did) } : null;
        delete e.room;
        const said = channel && e.body && e.body.room != null ? e.body.room : null;
        if (said) {
          const id = typeof said.id === "string" && said.id && said.id.length <= 200 ? said.id : null;
          // Who is in the room when the turn is handed out, from the channel. For a list only, what the entry says.
          const now = mint && id ? await toChannel(channel[1], "room", { id }) : null;
          const fresh = !!(now && now.known && Array.isArray(now.members));
          const list = fresh ? now.members : Array.isArray(said.members) ? said.members : [];
          const sure = (fresh || !mint) && id && (fresh ? now : said).complete !== false && list.length <= 50 && list.includes(address);
          const people = [];
          for (const a of list.slice(0, 50)) {
            const b = await boundOn(channel[1], a);
            people.push({ address: String(a).slice(0, 200), did: b ? b.did : null, role: b ? await roleOf(b.did) : null, handle: b ? await rows.get("handle/" + b.did) : null });
          }
          if (!sure) people.push({ address: null, did: null, role: null, handle: null });
          e.room = { id, name: String((fresh ? now.name : said.name) || "").slice(0, 100), served: !fresh || now.served !== false, people };
        }
        if (mint && role && !(e.room && !e.room.served)) e.turn = await turnToken.make(key, bound.did, e.id, { epoch, ...(e.room ? { room: [...new Set(e.room.people.map((p) => p.did))] } : {}) });
      }
      const headers = new Headers(r.headers);
      headers.delete("content-length");
      return new Response(JSON.stringify(data), { status: r.status, headers });
    });
  // Everything else goes to the core as it came.
  app.all("*", (c) => toCore(c));
  return app;
}

// %%
md`## Tests

The kernel runs under \`simulate\` with the core and the deployer replaced by recorders. Sign-in itself needs a PDS and is checked on a deployed kernel.`
// %%
kernelRig = async ({ core, secrets = { SESSION_KEY: "cookie-key", COOKIE_KEY: "cookie-key" } } = {}) => {
  const seen = [], toDeployer = [];
  const record = (list) => async (request) => {
    const body = ["GET", "HEAD"].includes(request.method) ? null : new TextDecoder().decode(await request.arrayBuffer());
    list.push({ url: request.url, method: request.method, headers: Object.fromEntries(request.headers), body });
    return request.url.endsWith("/go") ? new Response(null, { status: 302, headers: { location: "https://example.com/" } }) : Response.json({ ok: true });
  };
  const sim = await simulate(kernel_service, {
    secrets: { ...secrets, BRAIN_KEY: "kernel-key" },
    config: { host: "cb.sub.workers.dev", owner: "did:plc:owner", deployer: "https://cb-deployer.sub.workers.dev" },
    core: core || record(seen),
    deployer: record(toDeployer)
  });
  const B = "https://cb.sub.workers.dev";
  // session: a page's session token. bearer: any other token. cookie: sent as a cookie, which nothing reads.
  const call = async (path, { session, cookie, bearer, body, headers = {}, method } = {}) => {
    const r = await sim.fetch(B + (path.startsWith("/") ? path : "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain." + path), {
      method: method || (body === undefined ? "GET" : "POST"),
      headers: { ...headers, ...(cookie ? { cookie: "theme=dark; brain_session=" + cookie } : {}), ...(bearer || session ? { authorization: "Bearer " + (bearer || session) } : {}), ...(body === undefined ? {} : { "content-type": "application/json" }) },
      body: body === undefined ? undefined : typeof body === "string" ? body : JSON.stringify(body),
      redirect: "manual"
    });
    const text = await r.text();
    let data = text;
    try { data = JSON.parse(text); } catch {}
    return { status: r.status, data, headers: r.headers };
  };
  return { sim, seen, toDeployer, call, owner: await sessionToken.make("cookie-key", "did:plc:owner"), other: await sessionToken.make("cookie-key", "did:plc:other") };
}
// %%
test_the_signing_key_is_read_under_either_name = {
  const status = async (rig, token) => (await rig.call("/auth/session", { session: token })).status;
  const old = await sessionToken.make("cookie-key", "did:plc:owner"), fresh = await sessionToken.make("session-key", "did:plc:owner");
  // A Brain installed before the rename: only COOKIE_KEY is bound.
  expect(await status(await kernelRig({ secrets: { COOKIE_KEY: "cookie-key" } }), old)).toBe(200);
  // Only the new name.
  const renamed = await kernelRig({ secrets: { SESSION_KEY: "session-key" } });
  expect([await status(renamed, fresh), await status(renamed, old)]).toEqual([200, 401]);
  // Both names, one value: what a deploy sends from 2026-10-07.
  const both = await kernelRig({ secrets: { SESSION_KEY: "cookie-key", COOKIE_KEY: "cookie-key" } });
  expect(await status(both, old)).toBe(200);
  // Both names, two values: a session made under the old name is still read, and a new token is signed with SESSION_KEY.
  const split = await kernelRig({ secrets: { SESSION_KEY: "session-key", COOKIE_KEY: "cookie-key" } });
  expect([await status(split, old), await status(split, fresh), await status(split, await sessionToken.make("another-key", "did:plc:owner"))]).toEqual([200, 200, 401]);
  await split.call("people.put", { session: old, body: { did: "did:plc:alice" } });
  const made = (await split.call("portal.token", { session: old, body: { author: "did:plc:alice" } })).data;
  expect([!!(await portalToken.read("session-key", made.token)), await portalToken.read("cookie-key", made.token)]).toEqual([true, null]);
  // Neither bound: nothing is signed with an empty key.
  expect(await status(await kernelRig({ secrets: {} }), old)).toBe(401);
  expect((await kernel_service.emit()).meta.secrets.filter((n) => /^(COOKIE|SESSION)_KEY$/.test(n))).toEqual(["COOKIE_KEY", "SESSION_KEY"]);
  return "SESSION_KEY first, COOKIE_KEY still read";
}
// %%
test_session_token = {
  const good = await sessionToken.make("k", "did:plc:a");
  expect(await sessionToken.read("k", good)).toBe("did:plc:a");
  expect(await sessionToken.read("other", good)).toBe(null);
  expect(await sessionToken.read("k", good.slice(0, -2) + "xx")).toBe(null);
  expect(await sessionToken.read("k", await sessionToken.make("k", "did:plc:a", { ttl: -1 }))).toBe(null);
  expect(await sessionToken.read("k", good, 1)).toBe(null);
  const [, payload] = good.split(".");
  const forged = "v1." + btoa(JSON.stringify({ did: "did:plc:owner", exp: Date.now() + 1e6 })) + "." + good.split(".")[2];
  expect(await sessionToken.read("k", forged)).toBe(null);
  const rig = await kernelRig();
  expect((await rig.call("/auth/session")).data).toEqual({ signedIn: false, ownerSet: true });
  expect((await rig.call("/auth/session", { session: rig.owner })).data).toEqual({ signedIn: true, did: "did:plc:owner", handle: null, owner: true });
  expect((await rig.call("/auth/session", { session: rig.other })).data.owner).toBe(false);
  // The same value as a cookie is nobody: nothing a browser attaches by itself is read.
  expect((await rig.call("/auth/session", { cookie: rig.owner })).data).toEqual({ signedIn: false, ownerSet: true });
  expect((await rig.call("token.list", { cookie: rig.owner })).status).toBe(401);
  await rig.call("inbox.list", { cookie: rig.owner });
  expect(rig.seen.at(-1).headers["x-brain-caller"]).toBe("anonymous");
  // A session that has expired, or from before "sign out everywhere", is refused, not treated as nobody.
  expect((await rig.call("/auth/session", { session: await sessionToken.make("cookie-key", "did:plc:owner", { ttl: -1 }) })).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.call("/auth/logout?everywhere=true", { session: rig.owner, method: "POST" })).status).toBe(204);
  expect((await rig.call("/auth/session", { session: rig.owner })).status).toBe(401);
  return "signed, expiring, tied to an epoch, and not a cookie";
}
// %%
test_forged_caller_is_dropped = {
  const rig = await kernelRig();
  await rig.call("inbox.list", { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-key": "kernel-key" } });
  expect(rig.seen[0].headers["x-brain-caller"]).toBe("anonymous");
  expect(rig.seen[0].headers["x-brain-via"]).toBe("");
  await rig.call("inbox.list", { session: rig.owner });
  expect(rig.seen[1].headers["x-brain-caller"]).toBe("owner");
  expect(rig.seen[1].headers["x-brain-via"]).toBe("session");
  // The kernel proves itself to the core with its own key, not one the caller sent.
  expect(rig.seen[0].headers["x-brain-key"]).toBe("kernel-key");
  return "anonymous without a session";
}
